                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239251951",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198033250709",
                            "num_reviews": 113,
                            "playtime_forever": 645,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 645,
                            "playtime_at_review": 302,
                            "last_played": 1793996801
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Well made little puzzle game that uses simple and easily understood mechanics. Feels slightly on the harder side (coming from someone who is only so-so at puzzle games like this), but each level is relatively small and self-contained so getting stuck doesn't mean you have nothing to do. Level progression isn't purely sequentially locked (you instead unlock new levels like a tree branching out) so you can just play other levels instead and come back to the hard ones later.\r\n\r\nDifficulty curve didn't feel smooth to me but kind of offset but the branching-tree unlock making it not really matter (since you don't get truly stuck on individual levels). There are more levels than I expected, which I guess is better value for puzzle lovers since there's more to do lol.",
